    "body": "## Overview\n\nFail at startup when `--fingerprint-mode custom` is given without `--fingerprint-value`. Related open PRs #57399, #57390, #57436 cover mode `none`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- The server no longer starts silently with no `system_fingerprint` in responses when the custom value is missing or empty.\n\n## Validation\n\n`pytest tests/entrypoints/common/test_cli_args.py -k custom_fingerprint` (CPU, no GPU needed): the two new cases fail before (`DID NOT RAISE ValueError`) and pass after. `ruff check` and `ruff format` are clean.\n\n## Details\n\n`build_system_fingerprint` returns `None` for mode `custom` with no value, which behaves like mode `none`. The new check sits in `validate_parsed_serve_args` next to the other \"requires\" checks and needs a non-empty value.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/vllm-project/codesmith/vllm/pr/63814?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-